    "title": "014: The Relay and Away Mode (approval cards by email)"
  },
  "summary": {
    "kind": "quote",
    "span": {
      "end": 897,
      "end_line": 18,
      "line": 18,
      "start": 480
    },
    "text": "A build that needs a person's decision should be able to wait for them when they are away from the terminal, and they should be able to answer from wherever they are, without any of the properties of an approval card being weakened. This spec adds three things: a **relay scope** on the daemon, a **relay process** that carries cards out and answers back, and **parking** so an unanswered card does not fail the task."
  }
